This notice covers the films about MicroEngine and only them: "Seated", "Room
for another" and "Every step". They are NOT covered by the MIT License in the
root LICENSE file, which applies to the MicroEngine engine, its tools and
samples.

Covered (the "Films"):

  - media/seated/, media/room-for-another/ and media/every-step/: the
    compositions, scores and sound effects written as code, scripts,
    storylines, specifications and reviews;
  - media/LANDING-MOTION.md;
  - the rendered video files, wherever they are published, and the frames of
    them used as images on the MicroEngine website (site/src/assets/films/).

Not covered:

  - media/tools/ and media/films.json: the programs that build and publish the
    Films are part of the MicroEngine tools, under the MIT License.
  - The play shown in the Films, which belongs to the demo games and is
    covered by games/LICENSE, with the third-party files each game lists in
    its CREDITS.md under their own licences.
  - The typefaces (Bricolage Grotesque, IBM Plex Sans and IBM Plex Mono, SIL
    Open Font License 1.1), which are not kept in this folder: the build takes
    them from the website's packages. See THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md.

What you may do:

  - Watch the Films and link to them or embed them from where they are
    published.
  - Read and study their sources to learn how they were made, and view them
    and fork them on GitHub as GitHub's Terms of Service allow.
  - Build and render them on your own computer to learn.
  - Use the techniques and general ideas they show in your own, original work.

What you may not do without written permission from the copyright holder:

  - Redistribute the Films or their sources, whole or in substantial part,
    outside GitHub's fork feature.
  - Sell or otherwise commercialise them, or publish them, edited or not, as
    your own or as an endorsement of another product.

